A||||11||hugh||I need Sway bar help||||1||
Z||000000||hugh||04-01-2001||03:03 PM||||I need to replace the rear sway bar on my 88GT.The car weighs 3400lbs.2200 rear/1200front.Would a heavier than stock bar be better,and if so what bar might be a good choice?As long as it will reach the end links ,I can make the pieces necessary to mount it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||04-01-2001||05:02 PM||||You're better off going on how the car handles. Generally speaking, if the car pushes, (oversteers) the rear needs to be tighter, if the rear slides (understeer) then the front needs to be tighter. However there is a point where you will  achieve optimum handling. The true measure is if it's predictable, and controllable. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||04-01-2001||05:24 PM||||With your 65% rear weight bias, I would think that stiffer than stock rear springs and a stiffer FRONT bar would be indicated.<BR>Depends of course on what other suspension mods you've done, and where your CG height ended up.<BR>Gooooood luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||04-01-2001||10:01 PM||||If the car pushes it's called UNDERSTEER  If the back end comes around easily it's OVERSTEER||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||04-01-2001||10:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>I need to replace the rear sway bar on my 88GT.The car weighs 3400lbs.2200 rear/1200front.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do you keep lead bricks in your trunk? How do you get a Fiero to weigh that much?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||04-01-2001||11:56 PM||||Hey Hugh!<BR>So what is the car doing???<BR>Can you slide through a corner without the ass end coming around in front???<BR>Does the front not go where you point it???<BR>If the front and rear slide together, keep what ya got...<BR>If the front does not go where you point it, get a bigger bar in rear...<BR>If the ass end whips around, get a bigger bar in front...<BR>Do you need stiffer springs??<BR>Do you have poly???<BR>Is this a road car, or track car???<BR>How much do you want to spend!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||3400Fiero||04-02-2001||01:32 PM||||I have an Addco 1 inch rear sway bar if you are interested.  I put one on my car and it made a huge difference.  (I also have an oversize front bar)  Email me if you are interested.<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC||||reg||14
